import type { PaperBlock } from './types';

export const blocks: PaperBlock[] = [
  {"type": "callout", "label": "Foundational Thesis", "text": "Abstract The digital economy has learned to extract enormous value from human information. SunRey proposes a different architecture: make the individual the permission authority, make authorized contribution - not the person - the economic object, and make rights, purpose, provenance, verification and compensation machine-manageable without permanently publishing sensitive raw data. SunRey Coin is the native economic coordination asset for this human economic layer. Its underlying network, the Human Information Network (HIN), is not designed as a marketplace in people or a claim that personal data is collateral. It is designed as a rights-governed network in which verified human contribution can participate economically when a specific use is authorized."},
  {"type": "callout", "label": "Compensation", "text": "The canonical HIN sequence: economic participation begins with permission and verifiable contribution, not data possession."},
  {"type": "p", "text": "The architecture separates five things that conventional data markets often collapse: identity, information, rights, contribution value, and money. Sensitive source data can remain encrypted in a Personal Data Vault. A Purpose Firewall evaluates why an operation is requested. A Consent Ledger records granular authorization. Privacy Clean Rooms support computation-in-place. Proof of Contribution and provenance establish what occurred. The Personal Economic Value Engine (PEVE) estimates the market value of a specific authorized contribution. A separate monetary governance path determines whether and how native-asset settlement may occur. Core invariant Human worth is not contribution value. Contribution value is not SunRey Coin market price. Valuation is not monetary authority. Information may support an economic claim, but information alone cannot create money."},
  {"type": "callout", "label": "Core Principles", "text": "The Architecture in One Page SunRey treats human information as governed economic context rather than a resource that becomes monetizable merely because a platform possesses it. # Principle Architectural consequence The person is the permission authority Possession or technical access never implies permission to use information. Value the contribution, not the person The system evaluates a defined authorized contribution in a defined context. Raw data stays protected by default Sensitive source material remains in protected storage or controlled compute environments. Purpose is executable Every sensitive use declares requester, purpose, jurisdiction, duration, and permitted outputs. Verification precedes valuation A contribution must be attributable, evidence-backed, and unique before it can be economically valued. PEVE is not monetary authority A contribution valuation may inform compensation or a monetary proposal but cannot itself issue SunRey. One SunRey Coin remains one SunRey Coin The token remains fungible; contribution differences change compensation amounts, not per-owner token exchange value. Audit without publishing the dossier Evidence, rights, policy and settlement commitments can be anchored while sensitive source data remains off-chain. North-star design Put your money and your information to work for you - while preserving the individual as the center of the rights model."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "01", "label": "", "title": "Why a Human Information Economy Needs a New Rights Model"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "AI systems become more useful as they understand context. The strategic question is who controls that context, how it may be used, and who participates economically when it creates value. Traditional digital platforms frequently treat information collection, service access, analytics, advertising, model training and monetization as tightly coupled. The user may receive a service, but the economic rights surrounding downstream information use can be opaque. SunRey starts from the opposite direction: the existence of data does not create a blanket economic right to use it. The HIN is designed for a post-AI economy in which human intent, verified credentials, goals, preferences, authorized behavioral context, research participation and other contributions may be economically useful to enterprises and AI systems. But usefulness is not sufficient. The architecture requires a rights path: what is being requested, from whom, for which purpose, for how long, in which jurisdiction, under what privacy constraints, and with what compensation or participation terms? Design problem How can an economic network make human information useful to computation and markets without turning the individual into an irreversible data asset? The SunRey answer is to shift the scarce economic object away from the raw dossier and toward verified, purpose-bound rights and outputs. This makes permission, provenance, computation and compensation part of the economic transaction itself."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "02", "label": "", "title": "The Currency of You Thesis"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "\"The Currency of You\" does not mean pricing a human being. It means creating an economic layer in which people can authorize, verify and participate in the value created by specific contributions."},
  {"type": "callout", "label": "Settlement", "text": "A human-information economy requires a chain of authority, not a shortcut from data to token."},
  {"type": "p", "text": "SunRey Coin coordinates the human-information and participation economy. Representative sources of authorized economic activity can include verified credentials, research participation, professional and educational contribution, preferences and consumer intent, authorized financial context, user-declared goals, community participation, AI interactions, and permissioned outputs derived through controlled computation. The token is therefore positioned as a network coordination and settlement asset, not a claim of ownership over a person or their raw personal data. The intended value driver is useful network activity: rights transactions, rewards, compute requests, verified contribution, research participation, attestations, settlement and other authorized human economic activity. HIN principle Person → Permission → Verified Contribution → Authorized Economic Use → Compensation / Participation This sequence is the essential intellectual positioning. It places permission before economic use and contribution before compensation. It also creates explicit places for verification, privacy controls, policy and audit to operate."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "03", "label": "", "title": "Human Worth vs. Contribution Value"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "The Human Information Network is designed to reject the idea that the economic system should calculate an intrinsic score for a person. Age, health, DNA, psychology, location, social relationships and other sensitive characteristics do not become economic contributions merely because information about them exists. Where sensitive information participates in an authorized research or computation event, the monetizable object is the authorized contribution or computation event - not the underlying human characteristic. Concept Meaning Rule Human worth Intrinsic moral or social value of a person Outside the system; never computed. Personal attribute A fact or characteristic about a person Protected context; not automatically economic. Authorized contribution A specific act, dataset slice, credential, response, computation participation or verified output used for an allowed purpose Eligible for verification and valuation. Contribution value Context-specific economic estimate for the authorized contribution Calculated under a versioned methodology. SunRey Coin quantity A governed settlement or reward amount where permitted Downstream of valuation and monetary policy. SunRey market price Exchange value formed in permitted markets Separate from contribution valuation. Safety rule No protected trait, person-level desirability construct, social-credit concept or generalized human-worth score should become a shortcut into contribution valuation or token issuance."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "04", "label": "", "title": "Human Information Network Architecture"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "HIN is a permission-aware network that connects identity, rights, verified contributions, protected data, computation, provenance, valuation and compensation while preserving distinct authorities. Layer Function Identity & Participant Layer Login, wallet, pseudonymous human economic identity, enterprise identity, agent identity and governance identity. Vault & Protected Data Segmented encrypted source data and user-linked protected storage. Rights & Consent Granular rights grants, consent objects, purpose, duration, revocation, compensation and derivative-use terms. Personal Economic Graph Permission-aware relationships among authorized facts, goals, credentials, financial context and opportunities. Clean Room / Compute-to-Data Approved queries or models execute near protected data and return only allowed outputs. Contribution Registry Canonical contribution identity, provenance, uniqueness, challenge state and monetization state. Attestation & Evidence Source-specific verification, signed receipts, credential references, lineage and proof commitments."},
  {"type": "callout", "label": "Peve", "text": "Versioned valuation of a specific authorized contribution."},
  {"type": "p", "text": "SunRey Protocol Rights, policy, evidence and monetary governance determine permitted settlement and final state. Authority separation The HIN can observe, connect, verify and value. It is not a license for any database, AI model, oracle, frontend or analytics service to become monetary authority. WHO IS ACTING?"},
  {"type": "section", "n": "05", "label": "", "title": "Identity, Pseudonymity & Participant Separation"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "SunRey separates identities by function so public economic participation does not require unnecessary exposure of legal identity. Identity plane Purpose Boundary Login identity Access to SunRey applications and services. Authentication and session security. Wallet identity Addresses or custody references used for native-asset activity. May be multiple per human. Human economic identity Canonical participant identity used to attribute contributions and prevent duplication. Can be pseudonymous while linked to assurance evidence. Governance identity Identity permitted to participate in high-consequence protocol or policy decisions. Separate authorization and key controls. Enterprise identity Researcher, buyer, institution or service participant. Licensing, purpose and contractual state. AI-agent identity Registered software actor acting under a controller and capability limits. Cannot silently become the human or governance authority. A single human may control multiple wallets without multiplying a contribution. Contribution uniqueness attaches to the canonical participant/contribution event rather than to the number of accounts or addresses. This enables wallet flexibility while defending the economic layer against identity multiplication. Privacy objective Prove enough identity to establish attribution, rights and uniqueness - expose no more identity than the transaction requires."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "06", "label": "", "title": "Personal Data Vault & Raw-Data Isolation"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "Sensitive information should remain protected by default. SunRey is designed to move permissions and computation toward the data rather than routinely moving raw data toward every buyer or model. The Personal Data Vault is the protected source layer for categories such as identity, financial context, work and skills, consumption, user-declared goals, mobility, lifestyle and - only where lawful and explicitly authorized - health, wellness, biological or other sensitive data. The architecture is segmented so the existence of one category does not imply access to another. Control Objective Encryption & segmentation Separate sensitive categories and reduce the impact of compromise or overbroad access. Minimal disclosure Return only the attributes or outputs required for the authorized purpose. No public raw-data publication The blockchain can anchor hashes, rights, receipts, provenance and settlement evidence while source records remain protected. Controlled export User export or portability does not imply unrestricted marketplace resale. Retention & deletion controls Operational handling follows applicable rights and policy while finalized historical proof records remain append-only where required. Compute-near-data Clean-room execution can keep source material inside a controlled environment. Raw-data rule Sensitive personal source data is not the native on-chain asset. Rights, permissions, attestations, proof references and permitted outputs are the economic primitives."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "07", "label": "", "title": "Permission Authority & Consent Ledger"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "The HIN treats the individual as the permission authority. Authorization is a durable economic object, not a one-time interface checkbox. A granular consent object can specify the data categories, permitted purpose, requester, authorized compute, jurisdiction, duration, compensation terms, AI-training status, resale or derivative use, revocation rules and other constraints. This lets two requests for the same underlying information produce different outcomes because their purpose, scope or legal context differs. Consent field Economic meaning Data categories Exactly which sources or derived attributes are in scope. Purpose Research, product testing, analytics, personalization, advertising, AI training or another declared use - separately controlled. Requester Enterprise, researcher, agent, service or other identified actor. Duration Time-limited permission rather than indefinite possession. Jurisdiction Where the participant, requester and compute environment may operate. Compensation Minimum, clearing or agreed economic participation terms. Derivative / resale Explicitly allowed, constrained or prohibited. Revocation Stops future use where required; does not silently rewrite valid historical events. Rights principle A factual statement can be true while its use remains unauthorized. Truth and permission are separate states. WHY IS THIS USE ALLOWED?"},
  {"type": "section", "n": "08", "label": "", "title": "Purpose Firewall & Relationship Authorization"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "Possession of information never implies permission to use it. The Purpose Firewall makes that distinction executable. Every sensitive request should declare who is requesting, what information or relationship is requested, why it is requested, for how long, under which jurisdiction and policy, which model or agent will operate, and what output is allowed. The firewall then evaluates those dimensions against consent, product policy, legal capability and data sensitivity. Request class Example purpose boundary Research use May permit cohort eligibility or compute-to-data while blocking advertising and resale. Advertising use Can remain disabled even if the same information is permitted for another purpose. AI training Separately controlled; permission for inference or analysis does not automatically imply training rights. Financial personalization Can use authorized economic context under the user mandate without granting enterprise data-market rights. Monetary proposal Requires a distinct authorization path; permission for research does not automatically authorize a supply-changing use. Purpose firewall test What may be known? What may be used? By whom? For what purpose? For how long? In which jurisdiction? With which output and compensation terms?"},
  {"type": "section", "n": "09", "label": "", "title": "Personal Economic Graph"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "The Personal Economic Graph connects authorized facts and relationships so agents and economic services can reason over context without treating every known fact as universally usable. The graph can reference accounts, income, obligations, assets, debts, goals, skills, verified credentials, currencies, rewards, subscriptions, preferences, research eligibility, HIN contributions, SunRey participation and other authorized context. The graph should store or reference metadata that makes each relationship governable. Relationship metadata Question answered Source Where did the fact or relationship originate? Verification How strongly is it supported? Sensitivity What privacy treatment is required? Purpose For which uses may this edge participate? Consent state Is authorization current, expired, withdrawn or pending? Jurisdiction Which local rules and data-residency constraints apply? Permitted agent/model Which computational actors may use it? Expiry When must the authorization or fact be refreshed? Graph safety principle Knowing something never implies permission to use it. The Purpose Firewall and consent rules remain authoritative over the graph."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "10", "label": "", "title": "Privacy Clean Room & Compute-to-Data"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "A core HIN design move is to sell or authorize computation and defined outputs rather than indiscriminate copies of raw personal information."},
  {"type": "callout", "label": "Compensation", "text": "Compute-to-data: the buyer can receive a permitted result while raw sensitive data remains protected."},
  {"type": "p", "text": "A Privacy Clean Room receives an approved query, model or aggregation job; resolves the applicable participant cohort; verifies consent and purpose; executes against protected data; and releases only the allowed result. The result may be an aggregate statistic, eligibility proof, cohort count, model output, attestation or other defined artifact. Raw data access is false by default and any exception would require a separate high-control product. Stage Controls Input controls Approved model/query, signed requester identity, purpose, privacy budget, jurisdiction and data categories. Execution controls Isolated environment, policy enforcement, logging, output constraints and model/version references. Output controls Aggregation thresholds, permitted fields, privacy filters and evidence receipt. Economic controls Metering, contribution attribution, compensation rules and settlement evidence. Compute-to-data principle The economic object can be the right to compute or receive a verified output - not ownership of the underlying dossier."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "11", "label": "", "title": "Data Rights Packets"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "A Data Rights Packet (DRP) makes permissioned information markets legible by packaging exactly what can be used, how, where, and under which economic terms. DRP field Meaning Data categories The exact categories or derived attributes in scope. Cohort definition Eligibility conditions and minimum contributor count. Permitted purpose The specific allowed economic or research purpose. Authorized compute Allowed query, model or aggregation class. Raw data access Default FALSE. Jurisdiction Where participant, buyer and compute environment may be located. Expiry / revocation Time window and withdrawal handling. Compensation Minimum or clearing compensation; permitted settlement methods. Resale / derivative use Explicitly allowed or prohibited. Privacy budget Optional limits governing aggregate or model outputs. The DRP concept moves the marketplace from \"buy this dataset\" to \"acquire this narrowly defined, policyaware right.\" That shift is central to SunRey differentiation because it makes purpose, rights and privacy part of the market object rather than terms hidden in a separate contract. Market design Rights travel; raw sensitive data does not need to."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "12", "label": "", "title": "Contribution Attestation Mesh"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "Human contributions are not all verified in the same way. SunRey uses contribution-specific evidence classes rather than a single universal oracle. Contribution class Representative evidence Research Publication records, institutional evidence, study receipts, cohort participation, signed completion records. Education & skills Credential issuers, certificates, assessments and verified learning records. Work & professional contribution Employer, client or platform receipts; signed work artifacts; provenance and outcome evidence. Computation participation Signed job receipts, model execution receipts, usage metering and permitted-output records. Authorized information contribution Consent receipt, data-rights state, usage receipt, clean-room execution and output evidence. User-declared preferences/goals Self-attestation may be valid as a preference signal but does not automatically become independently verified fact. The mesh preserves provenance: which issuer, institution, provider or compute environment produced the evidence; how that evidence was transformed; what policy evaluated it; and whether independent corroboration was required. This creates a route from human participation to verifiable economic contribution without requiring one monolithic identity or oracle provider. Verification principle Self-attestation can be an input. It does not automatically become a verified economic fact where independent evidence is required."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "13", "label": "", "title": "Proof of Contribution & Canonical Contributions"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "Before a contribution can be valued, SunRey needs a durable answer to a basic question: what exactly happened once? Proof of Contribution is the evidence layer showing that an authorized contribution occurred, was attributable to the correct participant, was permitted for the relevant purpose, produced an eligible outcome, and has not already been monetized as the same event. The proof can reference hashes, consent state, usage receipts, output receipts, provenance and compensation without writing the underlying sensitive record to a public chain. Claim field Purpose Canonical participant Which human economic identity owns the contribution event? Canonical event identity What unique economic event occurred? Lineage Which sources and transformations support it? Rights references Which consent, rights and purpose objects authorized the event? Verification status What evidence class and confidence support the claim? Challenge state Is the claim accepted, disputed, under review or superseded? Monetization state Has this economic event already been compensated or used for an issuance proposal? Canonical claim Multiple observations can support one contribution. They do not automatically become multiple monetizable contributions."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "14", "label": "", "title": "Anti-Double-Counting & Sybil Resistance"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "The value layer must resist two distinct forms of inflation: duplicating the same contribution and multiplying identities around the same human participant. A research contribution might appear in a publisher database, university repository, researcher registry and aggregator. Those records can be four pieces of corroborating evidence for one contribution rather than four payable events. Likewise, one human may control multiple wallets; wallet multiplicity does not create multiple human economic contributions. Control Role Contribution fingerprinting Canonical event identifiers, source lineage and duplicate fingerprints identify repeated representations of one event. Participant uniqueness Human economic identity separates contribution attribution from wallet count. Credential assurance Credential references and identity assurance strengthen uniqueness without requiring public legal identity. Signed receipts Work, research, computation or data-use receipts establish specific completed events. Fraud signals Anomaly, velocity and relationship signals can escalate review without becoming automatic human-worth scoring. Challenge workflow Conflicting evidence can be disputed and resolved before value or compensation is finalized. Sybil principle A participant can have multiple accounts or wallets; the system should not allow those technical identities to multiply one human contribution."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "15", "label": "", "title": "Personal Economic Value Engine (PEVE)"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "PEVE is the valuation layer behind \"The Currency of You.\" It estimates the market value of a specific, verified and authorized contribution in a specific context. Illustrative canonical model Vh = f(D, S, V, F, U, P) - Cp - Cc, where D = demand, S = scarcity, V = verification quality, F = freshness, U = economic or research utility, P = permitted usage scope, Cp = privacy/sensitivity cost, and Cc = compliance cost. Earlier SunRey architecture work expands this research framework with completeness, geographic relevance and outcome contribution. The important point is not a fixed formula. It is the explicit separation of value drivers, privacy costs and compliance costs under a versioned methodology that can be calibrated, challenged and audited. Factor Question Demand How strongly does an authorized buyer or use case need this contribution? Scarcity How substitutable or rare is the relevant contribution in the eligible market? Verification quality How strong and independent is the evidence? Freshness How time-sensitive is the contribution? Utility What legitimate economic, analytical or research value does it create? Permission scope How broad or narrow is the authorized use? Privacy/sensitivity cost What additional safeguards, minimization or risk cost does the use require? Compliance cost What legal, operational and audit burden is associated with the use?"},
  {"type": "section", "n": "16", "label": "", "title": "Valuation Governance & Sensitive Categories"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "A contribution-value model can become dangerous if it quietly becomes a social ranking system. SunRey therefore treats methodology governance as part of the architecture. Each PEVE methodology should be versioned, explainable, calibrated against actual market behavior, subject to bias and sensitivity testing, and constrained by jurisdiction. Protected or highly sensitive traits should not become direct desirability multipliers. Sensitive categories warrant stronger purpose controls and privacy treatment, not automatic pressure for higher monetization. Governance control Requirement Method versioning Every valuation must identify the exact methodology and parameter version. Factor provenance Inputs should be traceable to authorized sources and evidence. Bias testing Methods should be tested for prohibited or unjustified proxy effects. Sensitive-category firewall Protected traits and human-worth constructs cannot become valuation shortcuts. Market validation Research values should be checked against real authorized demand rather than treated as intrinsic truth. Jurisdiction packs The same contribution may have different permitted uses or cost structures by location. Human review / challenge High-consequence valuations should support dispute, explanation and correction workflows. PEVE boundary PEVE can estimate contribution value. It cannot determine a person’s worth, set SunRey market price, or independently create SunRey supply."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "17", "label": "", "title": "SunRey Coin: Economic Role"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "SunRey Coin is the native economic coordination asset for the Human Information Network and broader human economic layer. Its role is to coordinate network participation rather than to collateralize a person or raw personal data. Depending on legal and product permissions, SunRey Coin can support settlement, rewards, network utility, information-market transactions, compute requests, attestation activity and other forms of authorized human economic participation. Economic role Illustrative use Contribution compensation A permitted settlement option for completed, rights-governed contribution. Research rewards Compensation or incentives for eligible research/product-testing activity. Network participation Rewards or utility associated with approved ecosystem contribution. Compute / information markets Settlement for authorized requests, metered computation or rights transactions. Transfers Native asset transfer where legally permitted. Exchange trading Market trading only where listing, custody and jurisdictional permissions exist. Access relationship Participation may influence governed Access entitlements, but Access remains a distinct noncash entitlement state. Not data collateral The intended value driver is useful network activity - not a simplistic claim that a person’s raw data \"backs\" the coin."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "18", "label": "", "title": "Fungibility, Compensation & Market Price"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "The architecture preserves fungibility: one SunRey Coin should not have a different exchange value because of who owns it. The \"economic value of you\" therefore affects the compensation basis for a specific authorized contribution, not the market exchange rate of each coin held by that participant. Two people can receive different quantities of SunRey for different contributions while the units themselves remain fungible once issued. Object Characteristics Economic treatment Contribution A High demand, scarce, strongly verified, narrow permission scope Higher contribution valuation may justify higher compensation under policy. Contribution B Common, lower-demand, less time-sensitive contribution Lower contribution valuation may justify lower compensation. SunRey Coin Fungible native asset Units do not carry owner-specific exchange values. Exchange price Market-clearing price in permitted venues Cannot be inferred directly from PEVE or a personal profile. This boundary avoids turning token ownership into a persistent personal score. It also allows the economic network to price authorized contributions dynamically while keeping the settlement asset legible for accounting, custody and exchange. Separation Contribution value determines what a contribution may earn. Market price determines what the fungible asset trades for. They are different mechanisms."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "19", "label": "", "title": "The Evidence-to-Money Firewall"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "The most important monetary safety principle is that no information system may silently become an issuance authority."},
  {"type": "callout", "label": "Issuance", "text": "Every stage can add evidence or interpretation; only the final governed protocol path may change native supply."},
  {"type": "p", "text": "Raw personal data cannot mint. An observation cannot mint. A verified economic fact cannot mint. A canonical claim cannot mint. PEVE cannot mint. An oracle, AI agent, API, frontend, exchange, identity provider, operational database or clean-room job cannot mint. These systems may create evidence, calculations or proposals; they do not possess sovereign monetary authority. Plane Authority Information authority Establishes what evidence exists and what claim is supported. Rights authority Establishes whether the evidence may be used for the requested purpose. Valuation authority Applies a governed method to estimate contribution value. Monetary policy authority Determines permitted conversion, caps, supply rules and other economic parameters. Protocol consensus Finalizes valid native monetary state transitions. Market Discovers exchange price after issuance; market price does not recursively authorize new issuance."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "20", "label": "", "title": "Governed Monetary Conversion & Issuance"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "Rights-governed evidence can become verified contribution; verified contribution can be valued; valuation can inform a governed conversion proposal. Those steps are intentionally separate."},
  {"type": "callout", "label": "Settlement", "text": "Canonical human-economy path. Production coefficients are governance inputs, not hard-coded assumptions."},
  {"type": "p", "text": "Production architecture should use typed, versioned economic parameter packages, explicit supply guards, conversion policy references, governance evidence and audit-ready policy commitments. Engineering fixtures or simulation values must never be promoted into production authority merely because a generic \"production\" flag is enabled. This preserves an important constitutional boundary: the software can be prepared to accept future tokenomics and conversion decisions without inventing those decisions. The current SunRey architecture intentionally leaves real production conversion coefficients and final issuance parameters subject to separate human governance, legal review and launch authorization. Monetary constitution Valuation is an input to policy. Policy is not a price feed. Price is not an issuance rule. Governance and protocol consensus remain the final authorities for supply-changing transitions."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "21", "label": "", "title": "Enterprise and Research Participation"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "The HIN becomes economically meaningful only when authorized buyers can request useful, bounded outputs under terms the participant can understand and control. Enterprise request Example HIN response Research cohort \"Find eligible participants matching defined criteria and run an approved analysis.\" Cohort rights + consent + clean-room compute + aggregate result. Credential verification \"Verify that this participant possesses a qualifying credential.\" Attestation or eligibility proof; no unnecessary credential dossier. Consumer demand intelligence \"Estimate demand among users who explicitly permitted this use.\" Purpose-scoped aggregate output with privacy threshold. Product testing \"Recruit authorized participants and compensate verified completion.\" Consent + task receipt + Proof of Contribution + settlement. AI evaluation \"Run an approved model against a permitted cohort without receiving raw records.\" Compute-to-data job + metered output + provenance receipt. This model creates a marketplace in narrowly defined rights and computation rather than downloadable dossiers. Enterprises gain clearer provenance and policy context; users gain visibility, revocability where applicable and an economic participation path; SunRey gains a network whose core transaction object includes purpose and rights. Demand-side rule Enterprise demand does not override user permission, privacy thresholds, legal capability or output constraints."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "22", "label": "", "title": "AI Agents Inside the HIN"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "AI can make the HIN more useful by finding relevant context, opportunities and relationships. It must remain subordinate to rights, policy and explicit capability boundaries. A SunRey Financial Agent may use the Personal Economic Graph to reason over authorized financial and personal context, identify a research opportunity, explain a potential economic benefit, or recommend that a user grant a specific permission. But the agent does not receive unrestricted access to every data category and does not directly move money or activate rights. AI dimension Rule Allowed AI role Classification, entity-resolution suggestions, opportunity discovery, explanation, anomaly detection, evidence summarization and user-facing analysis. Capability boundary Agent token defines allowed proposal types, data categories, accounts, amount limits, jurisdiction, expiry and revocation. Purpose boundary A model permitted for financial personalization may not automatically use the same context for advertising or training. Execution boundary AI proposes; deterministic policy and required human approval govern the action. Monetary boundary AI cannot authorize issuance, set monetary policy or elevate its own permissions. AI principle AI is an analyst and proposer - not the human, not the rights authority, and not the sovereign monetary authority."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "23", "label": "", "title": "Privacy, Security, Jurisdiction & Audit"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "A rights-governed information economy requires stronger evidence of control than a conventional \"privacy policy.\" The controls must be enforceable and reconstructable. Control Requirement Data minimization Collect or expose only what is required for the authorized purpose. Encryption & key separation Protected storage, distinct key purposes and workload-bound access. Purpose limitation Every sensitive operation is bound to a declared purpose. Jurisdiction state Location, legal entity, product capability and policy version are machine-readable. Immutable evidence Rights, policy, execution and compensation receipts support reconstruction of what happened. Revocation handling Stops future use as required while preserving append-only historical proof of previously valid events. Relationship authorization Access to a person, dataset or graph relationship does not grant unrestricted adjacent access. Red-team scope Privacy attacks, inference attacks, Sybil/economic attacks, application attacks and authorityescalation paths require dedicated testing. Trust proposition The HIN should be auditable enough to prove why a use was permitted without publishing the sensitive material that permission protected."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "24", "label": "", "title": "Illustrative Use Case I - Research Participation"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "A research organization wants to run an approved analysis on a cohort with defined eligibility characteristics. The SunRey architecture can support the request without transferring a raw user dossier. Step Stage What happens Buyer request Researcher declares cohort, purpose, model/query, jurisdiction, budget, output and reuse limits. Eligibility HIN identifies potentially eligible pseudonymous participants using authorized graph context. Consent Each participating user grants or confirms the specific research permission. Compute Approved job executes in a clean room near protected source data. Verification Execution receipts, data-rights state and outcome evidence form contribution attestations. Output Researcher receives the permitted aggregate or approved result, not unrestricted raw data. Valuation PEVE estimates the value of each eligible verified contribution under the applicable method. Settlement Compensation is paid in a permitted form; if SunRey is used, monetary conversion follows governed issuance/settlement rules. Proof Contribution, rights, policy, compensation and output receipts become auditable evidence. Result The researcher buys an authorized result. The participant retains rights over the underlying information and can participate economically in the completed use."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "25", "label": "", "title": "Illustrative Use Case II - Skills & Credentials"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "A participant has professional expertise and verified credentials. The economic network should distinguish the credential itself, proof of the credential, and any compensated contribution built on that expertise. For a simple eligibility request, the HIN may return an attestation that a credential threshold is satisfied without transferring the full educational or employment history. For a paid expert task, the contribution object becomes the completed task or verified output, supported by credential references, work receipts and provenance. Layer Example Credential source Issuer or trusted verification path establishes the credential reference. Permission Participant authorizes the requested verification or task context. Purpose Eligibility, expert recruitment, research or another defined use. Contribution Completed expert response, review, annotation, research task or other verifiable work. Attestation Signed receipts and output evidence support verification."},
  {"type": "callout", "label": "Peve", "text": "Demand, scarcity, verification, utility and permission scope inform contribution value."},
  {"type": "p", "text": "Compensation Fiat, SunRey or another permitted reward can settle the specific contribution. Privacy boundary Full employment history, legal identity or unrelated credentials are not automatically disclosed. Economic meaning Verified expertise can create value without creating a permanent score of the expert."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "26", "label": "", "title": "Illustrative Use Case III - Permissioned Consumer Intent"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "Consumer intent can be economically valuable, but SunRey treats it as an explicitly permissioned contribution rather than covert behavioral surveillance. A user may choose to share a purchase horizon, product category, travel interest, price sensitivity or another declared preference with a specific class of merchants or research buyers. The HIN can package that permission as a narrow rights object, enforce duration and purpose, and support aggregate market intelligence or targeted offers without granting open-ended access to unrelated behavior. Element Illustrative treatment User declaration \"I am shopping for an EV in the next 90 days.\" Permission scope Automotive offers and aggregate demand research; no unrelated advertising. Duration 90 days, renewable only by the user. Data access Declared intent + limited authorized context; raw unrelated transaction history stays protected. Compute Eligible merchants or research jobs receive a permitted score, cohort inclusion or offer route. Economic participation The user may receive an offer, reward, research compensation or other approved benefit. Revocation Future use stops when permission expires or is withdrawn, subject to applicable rules. Audit Receipts show which requester used which permission for which purpose. Difference from ad-tech The user declares the economic relationship and the purpose; the network does not assume that observed behavior is an unlimited asset for downstream use."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "27", "label": "", "title": "Network Effects & Economic Utility"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "The HIN network effect is stronger than \"more wallets create more value\" only if the architecture preserves trust and produces measurable utility for participants and authorized demand for buyers. Network effect Economic consequence More trusted participants Increase the breadth of authorized contribution and eligible cohorts. Richer permissioned context Improves agent personalization, research eligibility and enterprise computation. More enterprise/research demand Creates more compensated contribution opportunities and protocol utility. Better verification Improves confidence, reduces fraud and makes outputs more useful. Better rights tooling Lowers transaction friction for consent, purpose, jurisdiction and audit. More useful SunRey activity Increases legitimate settlement and network participation without requiring raw-data collateral claims. The moat depends on trust. If users perceive the HIN as surveillance or one-way extraction, the network effect reverses. The system therefore has to make permissions visible, revocation meaningful where applicable, compensation understandable, and data use auditable. Compounding loop Trust → participation → verified contribution → useful authorized outputs → compensation and better services → deeper trust."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "28", "label": "", "title": "Technical Differentiation & IP Prospects"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "SunRey does not need to claim invention of encryption, blockchains, clean rooms, identity systems or valuation algorithms individually. The differentiation is primarily in how these mechanisms are integrated as a rights-governed human economic architecture. Potential claim cluster Distinctive integration Rights-governed contribution pipeline Person → permission → verified contribution → authorized use → compensation, with explicit separation from human worth. Contribution-specific attestation mesh Evidence classes vary by research, work, education, compute and authorized information use. Canonical contribution + antiduplication Multiple evidence records resolve to one economic contribution and monetization state. PEVE + monetary firewall Versioned contribution valuation remains upstream of, but cannot directly control, native issuance. Compute-to-data rights packets Purpose, model, jurisdiction, output, privacy budget, compensation and derivative rights become machine-readable market state. Pseudonymous identity with economic uniqueness Separate wallet/login/governance identities while preserving participant-level anti-Sybil constraints. Proof-bound privacy model Evidence, rights and policy commitments explain economic settlement without publishing the raw dossier. IP caution These are technical differentiation themes, not legal conclusions on patentability. Formal claims require independent prior-art search and counsel analysis."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "29", "label": "", "title": "Governance & Production Boundaries"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "The architecture can encode constraints and evidence, but production rights, tokenomics, datamarket permissions and regulatory status require external decisions and human authorization. Boundary Required discipline Production monetary parameters Real conversion coefficients, issuance caps, supply policy and other tokenomics cannot be inferred from simulations. Legal classification SunRey Coin, compensation models, research markets and information-rights products require jurisdiction-specific analysis. Consent validity Technical consent objects must reflect applicable legal and contractual requirements. Sensitive-data use Health, biological, psychological, location and other high-sensitivity categories require the strongest legal and product controls. Enterprise data rights Provider licenses and buyer contracts must match the rights represented by the protocol. Security assurance Independent security review, key-management evidence, privacy testing and operational readiness remain launch gates. AI governance Model approval and monitoring cannot replace required human, compliance or governance approvals. Mainnet / live activation Code existence is not authorization to activate live financial, exchange or data-market capabilities. Production doctrine No single dataset, provider, AI model, operator, database, market price or software flag should be able to silently create economic or monetary authority."},
  {"type": "section", "n": "30", "label": "", "title": "Conclusion"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "The defining SunRey idea is not that a human being can be tokenized. It is that a human can become the authority over the rights surrounding their economic information and contribution. The Human Information Network turns this principle into architecture. Identity can be pseudonymous and function-specific. Sensitive source data can remain in protected vaults. Consent and purpose can be granular, time-limited and auditable. Clean rooms can bring approved computation to data. Contribution attestations and canonical claims can establish what occurred without multiplying the same event. PEVE can estimate the market value of a defined contribution without becoming a social score. SunRey Coin can provide a fungible coordination and settlement layer without claiming that the person or their raw data backs the asset. The most consequential design decision is the separation of authorities. Information may establish a fact. Rights determine whether it may be used. Verification determines whether the contribution is credible and unique. PEVE estimates economic value. Monetary governance determines what conversion, if any, is permitted. Protocol consensus establishes final monetary state. The market discovers exchange price. No single layer is allowed to collapse the others. Final thesis The Currency of You is a rights-governed economic architecture in which people can authorize, verify and participate in the value created by their contributions - without surrendering their identity, raw data, or human worth to the monetary system. For a post-AI economy, that is the larger proposition: human economic participation can remain first-class even as automation expands, provided the network values authorized contribution rather than treating people as data inventory."},
  {"type": "callout", "label": "Reference", "text": "Appendix A - Glossary & Source Basis Term Definition HIN Human Information Network - permission-aware network for verified human contribution, rights, computation and economic participation. SunRey Coin Native economic coordination asset for the human economic layer."},
  {"type": "callout", "label": "Peve", "text": "Personal Economic Value Engine - versioned valuation of a specific authorized contribution, not human worth. Personal Data Vault Protected segmented storage for user-linked sensitive source data. Purpose Firewall Authorization layer that determines whether a requested use is permitted for its declared purpose. Consent Ledger Granular, time-limited, revocable and auditable authorization state. Privacy Clean Room Controlled environment that executes approved computation near protected data and releases permitted outputs. Proof of Contribution Evidence that an authorized, attributable contribution occurred and produced an eligible economic outcome. DRP Data Rights Packet - machine-readable package of scope, purpose, compute, jurisdiction, privacy and compensation rights. Canonical Contribution Unique human economic event resolved across multiple observations and sources. Monetary Issuance Authority Governed protocol path permitted to finalize supply-changing native-asset transitions. Primary SunRey source basis  SunRey Comprehensive Business Plan - September 2026 (Sections 3-4).  SunRey Strategy, Product Architecture, Compliance Framework & Launch Valuation - August 2026 (Sections 3, 59, 14, 19-22).  SunRey Economic Awareness & Sovereign Monetary Architecture - September 2026 (Sections 2, 4-5, 7-9, 11-12).  Solstice Comprehensive Product, Architecture, API, Compliance & Growth Systems Report - August 14, 2026 (legacy naming; Sections 10-13).  Solstice SFF 2.0 Architecture Summary - August 2026 (PEVE and first-class economic intelligence components).  SunRey Blockchain & Universal Economic Exchange - Technical Architecture and Novel Market Design - August 2026.  SunRey Architecture & Production-Candidate Build Report - August 2026 (human-economy monetary constitution and permanent authority boundaries). Terminology note: historical Solstice/Pyramid references are normalized here to current SunRey naming where the concepts remain part of the present architecture. Technical and legal note: This paper is a conceptual architecture document, not legal, regulatory, securities, tax, investment or patent advice. Production capabilities require current jurisdiction-specific review, service-provider agreements, security approval, governance decisions and explicit activation."}
];
